  "title": "Harness Evolution in LLM Agents: A Behavior-Aware Framework",
  "summary": "Harness Evolution in LLM Agents: A Behavior-Aware Framework explores how model-harness co-evolution can enable recursive self-improvement in large language models. This framework addresses challenges in planning agents by leveraging behavior-aware learning and introduces a new approach for self-modifying agents.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The study introduces a unified taxonomy with nine design dimensions for evaluating recursive self-improvement (RSI) methods.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "It examines how existing RSI methods draw on traditional deep learning techniques like optimization, regularization, and adversarial learning.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The framework differentiates between capability-level and meta-level updates and reserves L5 for independently verified recursive gains.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
